Here, 👉 Shows how methods can return different data types.
----------------
addi() → returns int
ad() → void method (just prints, doesn’t return)
ap() → returns boolean
a() → returns String
----------------
👉 Since all methods are static, they’re called directly from main() without creating an object.

public class addition {
    public static int addi(int a, int b) {       // a, b are parameters 
        return a+b;
    }
    static void ad(int a, int b){
        System.out.print(a+b);
    }
    static boolean ap(int a){
        if(a>0){
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
    static String a(String p){
        return "name";
        
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int a = 10, b=11;
        char ch ='a';
        ad(a,b);
        System.out.println(addi(a, b));      // a, b are arguments which are passed with values
        System.out.println(a(null));
        System.out.println(ap(a));
    }
}
